{
 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "intro_cell",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Faradaic Efficiency (FE) Analysis\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook calculates the **Faradaic Efficiency (FE %)** of Formic Acid Decomposition (FAD) by selecting the reaction folder and aligning GC reaction rates with in-situ electrochemical current data, following the standard report generator architecture (`reaction_report.py`).\n",
    "\n",
    "### Electrochemical Principles:\n",
    "- **Formic Acid Anodic Oxidation**: $\\text{HCOOH} \\rightarrow \\text{CO}_2 + 2\\text{H}^+ + 2\\text{e}^-$ ($n=2$ electrons per $\\text{CO}_2$ molecule)\n",
    "- **Cathodic / Decomposition Hydrogen Generation**: $2\\text{H}^+ + 2\\text{e}^- \\rightarrow \\text{H}_2$ ($n=2$ electrons per $\\text{H}_2$ molecule)\n",
    "- **Faraday's Law**: \n",
    "  $$I_{\\text{theo}} = \\text{Rate} \\left(\\frac{\\text{mol}}{\\text{s}}\\right) \\times n \\times F$$\n",
    "  $$\\text{FE}_{\\text{CO}_2} (\\%) = \\frac{I_{\\text{theo, CO}_2}}{I_{\\text{measured}}} \\times 100 = \\frac{\\text{CO}_2\\ (\\text{nmol/min})}{\\text{Current}/2\\ (\\text{nmol/min})} \\times 100\\%$$\n",
    "  $$\\text{FE}_{\\text{H}_2} (\\%) = \\frac{I_{\\text{theo, H}_2}}{I_{\\text{measured}}} \\times 100$$\n",
    "  where $F = 96,485\\ \\text{C/mol}$."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "imports_cell",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import os\n",
    "import sys\n",
    "from pathlib import Path\n",
    "from datetime import date\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "import matplotlib.ticker as ticker\n",
    "from matplotlib.patches import Patch\n",
    "\n",
    "# Ensure project root and worker_files are on sys.path\n",
    "project_root = Path.cwd().resolve()\n",
    "worker_dir = project_root / \"worker_files\"\n",
    "\n",
    "for p in [project_root, worker_dir]:\n",
    "    if str(p) not in sys.path:\n",
    "        sys.path.insert(0, str(p))\n",
    "\n",
    "import config\n",
    "from worker_files.file_utils import select_folder_and_load_data\n",
    "from worker_files.electronics_worker import getcstats, calculate_gc_faradaic_efficiency\n",
    "from worker_files.GC_worker import calc_rxn_rates, compute_schedule_summary\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Loaded Faradaic Efficiency modules successfully!\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "folder_selection_md",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Step 1: Select Reaction Folder & Load Data\n",
    "Calls `select_folder_and_load_data()`, prompting you to choose the reaction folder just like in `reaction_report.py`. You can also specify `manual_dir` if you prefer to bypass the dialog."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "folder_selection_code",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Option A: Set a manual directory path (e.g. r\"S:\\projmon\\velma_formic-acid-decomposition\\Data\\...\")\n",
    "manual_dir = None\n",
    "\n",
    "if manual_dir:\n",
    "    selected_dir = Path(manual_dir)\n",
    "    dfs_dictionary, pre_reaction_df, _ = select_folder_and_load_data(selected_dir=selected_dir)\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    dfs_dictionary, pre_reaction_df, selected_dir = select_folder_and_load_data()\n",
    "\n",
    "if dfs_dictionary is None or selected_dir is None:\n",
    "    raise RuntimeError(\"No folder was selected. Please re-run this cell to select a reaction folder.\")\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"\\n[OK] Selected Folder: {selected_dir.name}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Path: {selected_dir}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Loaded datasets: {list(dfs_dictionary.keys())}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Set up data and plots output directories\n",
    "plots_dir = selected_dir / \"plots\"\n",
    "data_dir = selected_dir / \"data\"\n",
    "plots_dir.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n",
    "data_dir.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Load configuration metadata (YAML & Schedule sequence)\n",
    "try:\n",
    "    config.handle_yaml(selected_dir)\n",
    "    print(f\"[Config] Successfully loaded configuration for {selected_dir.name}\")\n",
    "except Exception as e:\n",
    "    print(f\"[Notice] Local YAML/sequence load notice ({e}). Checking project defaults...\")\n",
    "    # Fallback copy if files are absent in the target directory\n",
    "    if not list(selected_dir.glob(\"*.yaml\")):\n",
    "        default_yaml = project_root / \"reaction_meta_default.yaml\"\n",
    "        if default_yaml.exists():\n",
    "            import shutil\n",
    "            shutil.copy2(default_yaml, selected_dir / default_yaml.name)\n",
    "    if not list(selected_dir.glob(\"*sequence*.csv\")):\n",
    "        default_seq = project_root / \"sequence_default.csv\"\n",
    "        if default_seq.exists():\n",
    "            import shutil\n",
    "            shutil.copy2(default_seq, selected_dir / default_seq.name)\n",
    "    config.handle_yaml(selected_dir)\n",
    "\n",
    "RXN_SCHEDULE = config.RXN_SCHEDULE\n",
    "TRIAL_INFO = config.TRIAL_INFO\n",
    "GC_METHOD_INFO = config.GC_METHOD_INFO\n",
    "SHADE_COLORS = config.SHADE_COLORS\n",
    "\n",
    "p_reac_f = float(TRIAL_INFO.get(\"P reactor (psig)\", 0.0))\n",
    "v_box_t = float(GC_METHOD_INFO.get(\"Valve box T (deg C)\", 100.0))\n",
    "\n",
    "GC_df = dfs_dictionary.get(\"FAD_df\")\n",
    "raw_electronics_df = dfs_dictionary.get(\"electronics_df\")\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"GC data rows: {len(GC_df) if GC_df is not None else 0}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Electronics data rows: {len(raw_electronics_df) if raw_electronics_df is not None else 0}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "rate_calc_md",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Step 2: Calculate Reaction Rates & Extract Current\n",
    "- `getcstats()` processes raw electronics data, assigning continuous runtime, current, and scheduled voltage windows.\n",
    "- `calc_rxn_rates()` calculates molar gas rates ($\\text{CO}_2$, $\\text{H}_2$, $\\text{CO}$) from GC peak integrations."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "rate_calc_code",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# 1. Process continuous electrochemical measurements\n",
    "df_electronics = getcstats(\n",
    "    df_raw=raw_electronics_df, \n",
    "    file_path=None, \n",
    "    data_dir=None, \n",
    "    save_to_data_dir=False, \n",
    "    rxn_schedule=RXN_SCHEDULE\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "# 2. Calculate GC molar production rates\n",
    "rates_df = calc_rxn_rates(\n",
    "    GC_df=GC_df, \n",
    "    RXN_SCHEDULE=RXN_SCHEDULE, \n",
    "    v_box_t=v_box_t, \n",
    "    p_reac_f=p_reac_f, \n",
    "    GC_METHOD_INFO=GC_METHOD_INFO\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Preview of calculated reaction rates:\")\n",
    "preview_cols = [c for c in [\"Time (hr)\", \"Run\", \"Bias (V)\", \"Temp_C\", \"CO2 (nmol/min)\", \"H2 (nmol/min)\"] if c in rates_df.columns]\n",
    "display(rates_df[preview_cols].head())"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "fe_calc_md",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Step 3: Compute Faradaic Efficiency (FE %)\n",
    "`electronics_worker.calculate_gc_faradaic_efficiency()` aligns each GC sampling loop window with the corresponding potentiostat current to compute:\n",
    "- `Avg Current (mA)`\n",
    "- `FE_CO2 (%)`\n",
    "- `FE_H2 (%)`\n",
    "- `FE_Total (%)`"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "fe_calc_code",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Calculate instantaneous Faradaic Efficiency\n",
    "rates_df_fe = calculate_gc_faradaic_efficiency(\n",
    "    rates_df=rates_df, \n",
    "    df_electronics=df_electronics, \n",
    "    n_electrons=2, \n",
    "    gc_sampling_window_sec=60\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "fe_summary_cols = [\n",
    "    \"Time (hr)\", \"Run\", \"Bias (V)\", \"Temp_C\", \"N2_sccm\", \n",
    "    \"Avg Current (mA)\", \"CO2 (nmol/min)\", \"H2 (nmol/min)\", \n",
    "    \"FE_CO2 (%)\", \"FE_H2 (%)\", \"FE_Total (%)\"\n",
    "]\n",
    "avail_fe_cols = [c for c in fe_summary_cols if c in rates_df_fe.columns]\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"=== Instantaneous Faradaic Efficiency Data ===\")\n",
    "display(rates_df_fe[avail_fe_cols].head(20))\n",
    "\n",
    "# Export rates with FE to CSV\n",
    "fe_rates_path = data_dir / \"faradaic_efficiency_rates.csv\"\n",
    "rates_df_fe.to_csv(fe_rates_path, index=False)\n",
    "print(f\"\\n[Saved] Rates with Faradaic Efficiency saved to: {fe_rates_path}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Compute step-averaged summary (mean \u00b1 std)\n",
    "if \"Bias (V)\" in rates_df_fe.columns and \"Run\" in rates_df_fe.columns:\n",
    "    step_fe_summary = rates_df_fe.groupby([\"Run\", \"Bias (V)\", \"Temp_C\"], as_index=False).agg({\n",
    "        \"Avg Current (mA)\": [\"mean\", \"std\"],\n",
    "        \"CO2 (nmol/min)\": \"mean\",\n",
    "        \"H2 (nmol/min)\": \"mean\",\n",
    "        \"FE_CO2 (%)\": [\"mean\", \"std\", \"min\", \"max\"],\n",
    "        \"FE_H2 (%)\": [\"mean\", \"std\", \"min\", \"max\"],\n",
    "        \"FE_Total (%)\": [\"mean\", \"std\"]\n",
    "    }).round(2)\n",
    "    \n",
    "    print(\"\\n=== Step-Averaged Faradaic Efficiency Summary ===\")\n",
    "    display(step_fe_summary)\n",
    "    \n",
    "    step_fe_path = data_dir / \"faradaic_efficiency_summary.csv\"\n",
    "    step_fe_summary.to_csv(step_fe_path, index=False)\n",
    "    print(f\"[Saved] Step summary saved to: {step_fe_path}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "plotting_md",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Step 4: Faradaic Efficiency Plots\n",
    "1. **Faradaic Efficiency vs. Time**: Traces of $\\text{FE}_{\\text{CO}_2}$, $\\text{FE}_{\\text{H}_2}$, and $\\text{FE}_{\\text{Total}}$ with scheduled voltage bias shading.\n",
    "2. **Dual-Axis Rate Comparison**: $\\text{CO}_2$ gas production rate (nmol/min) plotted alongside measured electrochemical current (mA)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "plotting_code",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "colors = {\n",
    "    \"CO2\": \"#A10601\",     # Deep red\n",
    "    \"H2\": \"#2740CF\",      # Royal blue\n",
    "    \"Total\": \"#1A202C\",   # Dark slate\n",
    "    \"Current\": \"#059669\"  # Green\n",
    "}\n",
    "\n",
    "# ------------------------------------------------------------\n",
    "# PLOT 1: Faradaic Efficiency vs. Time with Bias Shading\n",
    "# ------------------------------------------------------------\n",
    "fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(11, 5.5))\n",
    "\n",
    "# Apply background bias shading\n",
    "if RXN_SCHEDULE:\n",
    "    for block in RXN_SCHEDULE:\n",
    "        if isinstance(block, dict) and \"time_window\" in block:\n",
    "            t0, t1 = block[\"time_window\"]\n",
    "            v = block.get(\"we_volt\", 0.0)\n",
    "            c = SHADE_COLORS.get(v, \"#ffffff\") if isinstance(SHADE_COLORS, dict) else \"#ffffff\"\n",
    "            ax.axvspan(t0, t1, color=c, alpha=0.9, zorder=0, lw=0)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Plot FE traces\n",
    "t_hrs = rates_df_fe[\"Time (hr)\"]\n",
    "ax.plot(t_hrs, rates_df_fe[\"FE_CO2 (%)\"], marker=\"o\", color=colors[\"CO2\"], label=r\"$\\text{FE}_{\\text{CO}_2}$ (%)\", lw=2, markersize=5, zorder=3)\n",
    "ax.plot(t_hrs, rates_df_fe[\"FE_H2 (%)\"], marker=\"s\", color=colors[\"H2\"], label=r\"$\\text{FE}_{\\text{H}_2}$ (%)\", lw=2, markersize=5, zorder=3)\n",
    "ax.plot(t_hrs, rates_df_fe[\"FE_Total (%)\"], marker=\"^\", color=colors[\"Total\"], label=r\"$\\text{FE}_{\\text{Total}}$ (%)\", lw=1.8, linestyle=\"--\", markersize=5, zorder=3)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Reference line at 100%\n",
    "ax.axhline(100, color=\"gray\", linestyle=\":\", alpha=0.7, lw=1.2, zorder=2)\n",
    "\n",
    "ax.set_xlabel(\"Time (hr)\", fontsize=13, labelpad=7)\n",
    "ax.set_ylabel(\"Faradaic Efficiency (%)\", fontsize=13, labelpad=7)\n",
    "ax.set_title(f\"Faradaic Efficiency vs. Time - {selected_dir.name}\", fontsize=15, pad=12)\n",
    "\n",
    "max_fe = rates_df_fe[\"FE_Total (%)\"].max() if not rates_df_fe.empty else 100\n",
    "ax.set_ylim(-5, max(120, max_fe + 15))\n",
    "ax.grid(True, linestyle=\":\", alpha=0.5, zorder=1)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Dual Legends: FE Lines & Bias Shading\n",
    "lines_h, labels_h = ax.get_legend_handles_labels()\n",
    "if RXN_SCHEDULE and isinstance(SHADE_COLORS, dict):\n",
    "    unique_biases = sorted(list(set(b.get(\"we_volt\", 0.0) for b in RXN_SCHEDULE if isinstance(b, dict))), key=lambda x: (isinstance(x, str), x))\n",
    "    bias_patches = [Patch(facecolor=SHADE_COLORS.get(b, 'white'), edgecolor='black', label=f'{b} V' if isinstance(b, (int, float)) else str(b)) for b in unique_biases]\n",
    "    leg1 = ax.legend(handles=lines_h, loc=\"upper right\", frameon=True, fontsize=10)\n",
    "    ax.add_artist(leg1)\n",
    "    ax.legend(handles=bias_patches, loc=\"upper left\", frameon=True, fontsize=9, title=\"Bias (V)\")\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    ax.legend(frameon=True, fontsize=10)\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "fig.savefig(plots_dir / \"Faradaic_Efficiency_vs_Time.png\", dpi=300, bbox_inches=\"tight\")\n",
    "plt.show()\n",
    "\n",
    "# ------------------------------------------------------------\n",
    "# PLOT 2: Rate Comparison (CO2 Production vs Measured Current)\n",
    "# ------------------------------------------------------------\n",
    "fig, ax1 = plt.subplots(figsize=(11, 5.5))\n",
    "\n",
    "ax1.plot(t_hrs, rates_df_fe[\"CO2 (nmol/min)\"], marker=\"o\", color=colors[\"CO2\"], label=r\"$\\text{CO}_2$ Rate (nmol/min)\", lw=2, markersize=5)\n",
    "ax1.set_xlabel(\"Time (hr)\", fontsize=13)\n",
    "ax1.set_ylabel(r\"$\\text{CO}_2$ Rate (nmol/min)\", color=colors[\"CO2\"], fontsize=13)\n",
    "ax1.tick_params(axis='y', labelcolor=colors[\"CO2\"])\n",
    "ax1.grid(True, linestyle=\":\", alpha=0.5)\n",
    "\n",
    "ax2 = ax1.twinx()\n",
    "ax2.plot(t_hrs, rates_df_fe[\"Avg Current (mA)\"], marker=\"d\", color=colors[\"Current\"], label=\"Measured Current (mA)\", lw=1.8, linestyle=\"-.\", markersize=5)\n",
    "ax2.set_ylabel(\"Measured Current (mA)\", color=colors[\"Current\"], fontsize=13)\n",
    "ax2.tick_params(axis='y', labelcolor=colors[\"Current\"])\n",
    "\n",
    "h1, l1 = ax1.get_legend_handles_labels()\n",
    "h2, l2 = ax2.get_legend_handles_labels()\n",
    "ax1.legend(h1 + h2, l1 + l2, loc=\"upper left\", frameon=True, fontsize=10)\n",
    "plt.title(f\"$\\text{CO}_2$ Production vs. Electrochemical Current - {selected_dir.name}\", fontsize=14, pad=12)\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "fig.savefig(plots_dir / \"CO2_Rate_vs_Current.png\", dpi=300, bbox_inches=\"tight\")\n",
    "plt.show()\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"All plots exported successfully to: {plots_dir}\")"
   ]
  }
 ],
